# `SKILL_NAME` — ONE_LINE_PURPOSE

What this skill owns, and what it deliberately does not. State the boundary against
adjacent skills so they do not cross-trigger.

Entry points live next to this file. Resolve them as
`~/.agents/skills/SKILL_NAME/lib/<entry>.py`.

Python is the only source language for skill scripts — no shell. Shared primitives
(process spawning, output, paths, git, tmux, tuicr) come from the shared
`~/.agents/skills/_lib/skillkit` package; read `_lib/README.md` before adding one.

## Quick start

```bash
~/.agents/skills/SKILL_NAME/lib/<entry>.py <args>
```

## Workflow

1. Step → verify: how you know the step worked
2. Step → verify: how you know the step worked

## Gotchas

Environment-specific facts that defy reasonable assumptions. Record the corrections a
human had to make, not general advice.

